course: dictionary
lesson: 5644
title: Lint: tiny fluff and old cotton cloth
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Lint is tiny bits of fluff and fibre that come off clothes and cloth. You may find it in your pockets, or as grey specks on a dark jumper. Good readers notice that the word is about very small things.
explain: «The tumble dryer's lint filter should be cleaned after each use, because fluff can start a fire.» The words around lint give you clues. The filter is where the fluff collects, and fluff is the meaning that fits. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence.
explain: Lint has a second meaning too: soft cotton cloth once used to cover wounds. To choose the right meaning, read the sentence around it. If it talks about dryers, pockets or jumpers, lint means fluff. If it talks about cuts, wounds or bandages, lint means cloth.
fact: Lint is tiny bits of fluff and fibre that come off clothes and cloth.
fact: Lint collects in a tumble dryer's lint filter, in pockets and on dark clothes.
fact: The lint filter is the part of a tumble dryer that catches lint, and it must be cleaned out.
fact: Lint in a dryer can catch fire, so clean the filter after each use.
fact: Lint can also mean soft cotton cloth once used to cover wounds.
exercise: What is lint? | A dark, woolly jumper | A kind of tumble dryer | *Tiny bits of fluff and fibre that come off clothes | A small, hard stone found in a pocket
exercise: «The tumble dryer's lint filter should be cleaned after each use, because fluff can start a fire.» Why must the lint filter be cleaned? | It is dirty and smells bad | It makes the clothes wet | *Lint can catch fire if it builds up | It keeps the dryer cold
exercise: «The nurse covered the cut with soft lint.» What does lint mean here? | Fluff from a jumper | A tiny stone | A roller for clothes | *Soft cotton cloth for a wound
test: Which phrase names a roller that picks up fluff from clothes? | *Lint roller | Belly button lint | Pocket lint | Lint filter
test: What does lint mean in «belly button lint»? | A stone in the belly | *Tiny fluff from clothes | A kind of button | Soft cotton cloth
exam: Which sentence uses lint to mean soft cotton cloth for a wound? | «The lint filter is full.» | «I found pocket lint on my jumper.» | «The dark jumper was covered in lint.» | *«The nurse pressed lint onto the cut.»
